sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: x402 failure: the payer balance is too low
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: x402 failure: the payer balance is too low. 4 participants: Client (agent), Resource server, Facilitator, and Base Sepolia. 6 steps, 2 crossing a trust boundary, 1 failure branch. Based on x402 v2.0 (2025-12-09). Step 1: Client (agent) to Resource server: Retry with PAYMENT-SIGNATURE. Step 2: Resource server to Facilitator: POST /verify. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 3: Facilitator to Resource server: Return isValid false (insufficient_funds). If The balance was enough at verify time but dropped before settle: Verify passes and the handler runs. Steps 4 to 6 show the settle-time variant. Step 4: Resource server to Facilitator: POST /settle (balance dropped after verify). This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 5: Facilitator to Resource server: Return success false (insufficient_funds). Step 6: Resource server to Client (agent): 402 with PAYMENT-RESPONSE success false.
  autonumber
  participant p_client as Client (agent)
  participant p_server as Resource server
  participant p_facilitator as Facilitator
  participant p_chain as Base Sepolia
  p_client->>p_server: Retry with PAYMENT-SIGNATURE
  p_server->>p_facilitator: POST /verify
  Note over p_server,p_facilitator: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_facilitator-->>p_server: Return isValid false (insufficient_funds)
  else The balance was enough at verify time but dropped before settle
    Note over p_facilitator,p_server: Verify passes and the handler runs. Steps<br/>4 to 6 show the settle-time variant.
  end
  p_server->>p_facilitator: POST /settle (balance dropped after verify)
  Note over p_server,p_facilitator: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_facilitator-->>p_server: Return success false (insufficient_funds)
  p_server-->>p_client: 402 with PAYMENT-RESPONSE success false
